liberty under the guise of combating terrorism.  So far, this approach is working like a charm, so I doubt we&#39;ll see a change in tactics any time soon.&lt;BR/&gt;Got your book yesterday, Will.  Great work!</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/8418487781097681154'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/8418487781097681154'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html?showComment=1200507840000#c8418487781097681154' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4082587910498177714' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/4082587910498177714' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="January 16, 2008 at 11:24 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4439994920837372528</id><published>2008-01-16T06:38:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2008-01-16T06:38:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>In a time when our gov&#39;t can&#39;t seem to decide whet...</title><content type='html'>In a time when our gov&#39;t can&#39;t seem to decide whether waterboarding, sleep deprivation, isolation, temperature extremes, etc. are torture - if we do it - I don&#39;t really see them being inclined to be supportive of our 2nd amendment rights.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/4439994920837372528'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/4439994920837372528'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html?showComment=1200490680000#c4439994920837372528' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4082587910498177714' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/4082587910498177714' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="January 16, 2008 at 6:38 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4556158403225752788</id><published>2008-01-16T05:33:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2008-01-16T05:33:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>&quot;April 19, 1775: Anti-government extremists riot, ...</title><content type='html'>&quot;April 19, 1775: Anti-government extremists riot, firing on the constabulary sent to enforce a ban on illegal assault weapons.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;That&#39;s exactly how the events of 1775 would be described in British America&#39;s history texts, had the &#39;colonial rebellion&#39; failed. It would be a mere footnote, as obscure as the Whisky Rebellion.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;Like every other revolutionary government, the U.S. has experienced a counter-revolution. Nearly every radical notion of the late revolution, such as the extreme emphasis on individual liberty, has been nullified or inverted in the present day. Gaping contradictions between constitutional principles and everyday statutes produce little cognitive dissonance in the minds of lawyers, much less the general public.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The Supreme Court is made up of lawyers, anxious to advance the interests of their profession -- more laws, more litigation, more legal jeopardy. Accordingly, even if the Court finds an individual right to bear arms in the Second Amendment, it will surely qualify it with a safe harbor for &#39;reasonable regulation&#39; at the state and local level. Even Washington DC&#39;s draconian restrictions on firearms might make the grade as &#39;reasonable,&#39; with some minor tweaking.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;In other words, &quot;No contradiction here, folks! It&#39;s ALL CONSTITUTIONAL.&quot;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The agenda, of course, is to maintain the morass of 20,000-plus federal, state and local regulations, which provide a fertile minefield for prosecutors and defense lawyers. When even the most informed, punctilious gun owner can get tripped up on an obscure paperwork or status violation and face years in jail, smiles light the faces of the black-robed justices. After all, if justice was simple, even a layman could figure it out. The horror, the horror!</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/4556158403225752788'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/4556158403225752788'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html?showComment=1200486780000#c4556158403225752788' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4082587910498177714' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/4082587910498177714' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="January 16, 2008 at 5:33 AM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4023582191864019393</id><published>2008-01-15T22:01:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2008-01-15T22:01:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>Zachary -- Yes, Liberty in Eclipse will soon be av...</title><content type='html'>Zachary -- Yes, Liberty in Eclipse will soon be available at Amazon, B&amp;N and other retailers. I&#39;ll keep you updated.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/4023582191864019393'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/4023582191864019393'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html?showComment=1200459660000#c4023582191864019393' title=''/><author><name>William N. Grigg</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/14368220509514750246</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='25' height='32' src='http://www.weekendinterviewshow.com/pics/grigg.jpg'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4082587910498177714' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/4082587910498177714' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-1344012943"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="January 15, 2008 at 10:01 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-7064381478682584238</id><published>2008-01-15T19:23:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2008-01-15T19:23:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>I&#39;m not finding your book on amazon or B&amp;N, etc, b...</title><content type='html'>I&#39;m not finding your book on amazon or B&amp;N, etc, but I trust it will be there soon? &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;The Bush administration also gave its  2 cents the other day. It seems that they, the ADL, and other fascist organizations are overly concerned with the demise of &quot;gun control&quot; in general. For some reason, they fear the SCOTUS will rule according to the constitution, thereby imperiling all federal laws, and not simply DC&#39;s. Indeed, as any honest and literate person would know, the 2 amendment simply means that the Federal government may not make any  gun laws for the states or the people. Such an honest reading would suddenly leave a thousand DOJ (sic) ATF jackboots out of work, and we know that government never shrinks or relinquishes power in such a manner. No, the court is only speaking to this question: are the rights of individuals not on duty with the national guard infringed by not being allowed to possess handguns or long guns for  self-defense.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;I believe that if the court answers in the negative, that many people will become agitated and mobilized in way that will be shocking and refreshing. For this reason, perhaps it would be best for a negative answer. Really, if the court says essentially &quot; The second  amendment gives the government the right to keep and bear arms&quot; what would be the legitimate use of the Judicial Branch? If that&#39;s what the court says and we accept it, then it&#39;s time to look elsewhere. At least most of the rest of the world has the integrity to scoff at the idea of an armed citizenry!!!</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/7064381478682584238'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/7064381478682584238'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html?showComment=1200450180000#c7064381478682584238' title=''/><author><name>Zachary</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/05334525584242029389</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4082587910498177714' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/4082587910498177714' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-995279443"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="January 15, 2008 at 7:23 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-6710900762845063128</id><published>2008-01-15T19:13:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2008-01-15T19:13:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>The &quot;Fatal Embrace&quot; is a must read and shows peopl...</title><content type='html'>The &quot;Fatal Embrace&quot; is a must read and shows people don&#39;t learn from history. &lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;A libertarian fellow has both the ADL  and the AJC press releases here:&lt;BR/&gt;http://www.nolanchart.com/article1124.html&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;This is from the American Jewish Committee press release on their filing of an amicus brief.&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;B&gt;AJC has a long history of supporting gun control laws, including the federal Gun Control Act of 1968, the federal Assault Weapon Control Act of 1989, and the Brady Handgun Prevention Act of 1993.&lt;/B&gt;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/6710900762845063128'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/6710900762845063128'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html?showComment=1200449580000#c6710900762845063128' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2008/01/adls-holocaust-denial.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-4082587910498177714' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/4082587910498177714' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-262634513"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="January 15, 2008 at 7:13 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3077926284115227722</id><published>2008-01-15T18:40:00.000-07:00</published><updated>2008-01-15T18:40:00.000-07:00</updated><title type='text'>Upon viewing the picture of Mark P. (of the ADL) i...</title><content type='html'>Upon viewing the picture of Mark P. (of the ADL) it is clear he has in great need of a physical work out. A textbook example of a state sponsored parasite. Look at that lard ass. Its disgusting</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/3077926284115227722'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/4082587910498177714/comments/default/3077926284115227722'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedo